# R9, log lines 163..167 (5 commits).

# moved: 8d9f0c7b35 pulled earlier past b7f4a9c3e2 (tools/build/watched-run.raku
# only); it touches the two Makefile templates the trim commit already edits.
= Trim the legacy Perl6 frontend: RakuAST is the only frontend
World/Actions/Grammar and rakudo-debug leave the build: src/main.nqp is RakuAST-unconditional
and loads modules through ModuleLoader, the desugars the legacy frontend carried move to
src/vm/jvm/Raku/Ops.nqp, and the Makefile templates lose the frontend's build rules, the
now-inert ones included.
- 59326c65ae Trim the legacy Perl6 frontend (World/Actions/Grammar + rakudo-debug) from the build
- 8d9f0c7b35 Remove the inert build rules for the trimmed legacy frontend

= keep
- b7f4a9c3e2 watched-run: mirror the elapsed [Ns] --show markers into the log

= eval-server: libgraal-sized cage, heap uncommit, bounded child JVMs
The memory cage accounts for libgraal's native footprint and the heap is uncommitted between
runs, so a single warm server survives a whole subdirectory; the JVM children a spawn-heavy
test forks are bounded. AGENTS.md drops its hand-rolled memory-guard guidance.
- 2de3ca91c4 eval-server: size the cage for libgraal and uncommit the heap
- 8f22859438 eval-server: bound the JVM children a spawn-heavy test forks
